            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How do you handle an initial start up of the BMC vs a restart of the service (such as when it crashes)?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "It should be the same work. The init handlers would need some logic to avoid duplication. For example the following condition:\n1. stuff broken. active high GPIO asserts.\n2. RISING handling calls the assert sd service.\n3. stuff continues to be broken. BMC restarts or someone restarts gpiod service.\n4. INIT_HIGH gets called, calls the new target.\n\nThe new target has to ensure that the new condition is not already reported/handled. Else if it does the not-so-smart-stuff. Unless we want to through those smarts into PGM?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
